<title>GERMANY: German traders seek free market wheat, rye exports.</title>
<headline>German traders seek free market wheat, rye exports.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German grain traders are seeking export restitutions for the export of 13,800 tonnes of free market soft wheat in a range between 8.29 and 13.99 Ecus per tonne, state grain intervention board BLE said.</p>
<p>Traders at the weekly EU grain export tender also sought rebates for the export of 50,000 tonnes of free market rye at 44.89 Ecus/tonne.</p>
</text>
